version: 2.0.1-ncomms
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/StatXzy7/SFibAI"
abstract: >-
  Official code repository for SFibAI, a deep learning system for automated,
  fine-grained grading of Schistosoma japonicum-induced liver fibrosis in
  ultrasound images. Trained and evaluated on a multicentre dataset of 167,702
  ultrasound images labelled on a 36-level scale (0.0-3.5) that maps onto the
  four clinical grades (F0-F3), the system achieves a mean absolute error of
  0.116 with 93.9% of predictions within 0.5 grades on an independent test set
  of 16,811 images, and a deployable version processes each image in under
  400 ms on Windows and Android devices.
keywords:
  - liver fibrosis
  - schistosomiasis
  - ultrasound
  - deep learning
  - radiomics
  - computer-aided diagnosis
  - schistosomiasis japonica
  - fibrosis grading
  - reproducibility
